Pinned jj-hunk-tool 817a3d19: normalize sliced outer context for GNU patch.

Slicing can turn unselected changes into 16 leading vs 3 trailing context
lines. GNU patch treats the imbalance as a boundary hint and rejects exact
interior matches. Share generation between preview and mutation, retaining
min(3, leading, trailing) outer context without changing selections or IDs.
Recompute starts/counts, including zero-length unified-diff anchors.

Tests cover both asymmetries, forward/reverse, BOF/EOF, zero counts, disjoint
and one-sided selections, unchanged IDs, GNU patch --fuzz=0, and real jj squash.
The actual GNU patch invocation and its fuzz setting are unchanged.

